brcmfmac D3 suspend/resume fix for Apple T2 Macs
=================================================

Patched pcie.c for brcmfmac (Linux 6.18.5) targeting BCM4364/BCM4377
on Apple T2 MacBooks (MacBookPro15,x / 16,x).

What it does
------------
- Deep sleep state machine tracking for D3 entry/exit
- Hot resume with D0_INFORM + firmware health check (BRCMF_C_UP)
- Cold resume fallback: full remove + reprobe when firmware is dead
- TCM validation before and after resume to detect firmware crashes
- Post-resume settle delay for firmware re-initialization
- Verbose suspend/resume logging via pr_info

Module parameters
-----------------
  force_cold_resume   Force cold recovery on every resume (bool, default 0)

Build
-----
  cp pcie.c <kernel-src>/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
  KDIR=/usr/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build
  make -C $KDIR M=<kernel-src>/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211 modules

Install
-------
  sudo cp brcmfmac/brcmfmac.ko /usr/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/updates/
  sudo depmod -a
  sudo modprobe -r brcmfmac && sudo modprobe brcmfmac

Tested on
---------
  MacBookPro16,1 — BCM4364/4 (b3), PCI 14e4:4464
  Kernel 6.18.5-arch1 (Arch Linux T2)

Should also work
----------------
  BCM4377-based T2 Macs (not tested)

Base kernel
-----------
  https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git v6.18.5
